  "summary_en": "Minnesota statute regulating law enforcement use of unmanned aerial vehicles: warrant requirement with enumerated exceptions, bans on weapons and unwarranted facial recognition, data classification and seven-day deletion, public comment, written policies, documentation, and annual reporting.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Law enforcement must obtain a search warrant to use a UAV, except for eleven listed authorized uses.",
   "UAVs may not be armed or use facial recognition/biometric matching without a warrant.",
   "UAV data is private and must be deleted within seven days unless part of an active investigation.",
   "Unlawfully obtained UAV information is inadmissible and aggrieved parties may sue.",
   "Agencies must adopt public written policies, allow public comment, and file annual reports."
